# Old-domain redirect for a domain migration (docs/runbooks/domain-migration.md).
# Copy to old-domain.caddy, replace the hostname, `docker compose up -d`.
#
# `redir ... {uri} 308` forwards the full path AND query string, so every
# previously shared https://old-host/s/<id> link lands on the same capture at
# the new host; 308 (not 301/302) keeps the method for API clients. Caddy
# manages a certificate for this name as long as the block exists and DNS for
# it still points here — remove the block only when you are ready for old
# links to stop working (see the runbook's redirect-lifetime section).
old.shots.example.com {
	redir https://{$PUBLIC_HOST}{uri} 308
}
